	)
	(text "PIN RESTRICTIONS (ST DS13560)\n(!) PA8  may read LOW during reset/boot: UCPD\n     dead-battery pull-down, set by PA9's level.\n     Released when firmware strobes (F1).\n(!) PC15 RTC-domain pin: sinks ≤ 3 mA, ≤ 2 MHz,\n     ≤ 30 pF; must NOT source current (no LED).\n(!) PA4/PA5 are TT pins: 3.6 V max (not 5 V\n     tolerant). PA6/PB3: no negative injection.\n(!) PA9/PA10 = UCPD DBCC pins: a HIGH level here\n     enables PA8's dead-battery pull-down (F1).\n(!) U1 pins 22/23 are named 'PA9/PA11',\n     'PA10/PA12' in ST's symbol: remappable pads,\n     used as PA11/PA12. Leave the remap off.\n\nFIRMWARE RULES\nF1  SystemInit(): set SYSCFG_CFGR1.UCPD1_STROBE\n     and UCPD2_STROBE first (frees PA8).\nF2  USB unused: keep the USB peripheral and its\n     D+ pull-up (USB_BCDR.DPPU_DPD) OFF.\nF3  Production: verify nBOOT_SEL = 1, nBOOT0 = 1;\n     power-cycle after the first flash. RDP1 blocks\n     the ST bootloader (updates = mass-erase +\n     reflash, or a custom IAP). Never RDP2.\nF4  Buzzer: TIM4 PWM only; idle LOW, never DC.\nF5  VSENSE: buzzer silent, ≤ 10 kSps, × 3.\nF6  Clock: HSEBYP while HSEON = 0, then HSEON;\n     PLLM = 2, PLLN = 32, PLLR = 2, PLLQ = 2.\nF7  CSS on. In the CSS NMI set PB1 (CAN_TX) to\n     input first (R15 = recessive), then re-init.\nF8  FDCAN NBTP = value − 1: NBRP 7, NTSEG1 12,\n     NTSEG2 1, NSJW 1.\nF9  Never enable LSE / PC15 AF0-1; keep NRST\n     bidirectional; enable BOR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 317.5 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "75f7d392-8a78-4ac6-a4c6-11879f9395d9")
	)
	(text "DECOUPLING  (U1 pin 4 = VDD/VDDA, pin 5 = VSS)\n• C4 100 nF: supplies the fast current spikes each time the\n   core and I/O switch (MHz). Must sit right at pin 4.\n• C5 10 µF 0805 (≈ 6.9 µF at 3.3 V): bulk reservoir for slower\n   load steps (ST AN5096 asks for ≥ 4.7 µF).\n• Placement: C4 closest to pin 4 (≤ 2 mm), C5 just behind it;\n   each with its own via straight down to the GND plane.\n\nRESET  (NRST, U1 pin 6 → M.2 pin 11)\n• NRST is active-low: 0 V = reset, 3.3 V = run. Internal ~40 kΩ\n   pull-up to 3.3 V, so no external resistor is needed.\n• C6 100 nF to GND is a noise filter: the NRST trace runs to the\n   M.2 fingers / ST-Link cable and picks up spikes and ESD. A\n   spike couples in through only a few pF, so against 100 nF it\n   barely moves NRST: no accidental reset. After a real reset\n   the 40 kΩ pull-up recharges C6 in ≈ 5 ms (3–7 ms).\n• Real resets (ST-Link, carrier button NRST → GND) hold the pin\n   low long enough to drain C6. C6 also debounces the button.\n• Everything on NRST may only pull LOW (open-drain, wired-OR).\n   Never drive it high, never add more capacitance — the STM32's\n   own ~20 µs reset pulse must still pull it fully low.\n• C6 ≤ 2 mm from pin 6, short via to GND.  (MES4-CIF §4a)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "87283df0-e996-457c-aebb-1a0ac5895c4c")
	)
